   "help": "The B code follows the lesion and, for encapsulated and solid papillary carcinoma, the invasion field (RCPath G150, 2026). A B category chosen below still wins.",
   "reference": {
    "title": "Papillary lesions on core biopsy",
    "intro": "B codes follow RCPath G150 (2026). Myoepithelial cells, CK5/6 and ER separate benign from atypical and malignant papillary lesions (Kulka 2022).",
    "columns": 3,
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "Intraductal papilloma (B3)",
      "points": [
       "Fibrovascular cores lined by epithelial and myoepithelial cells",
       "p63: myoepithelial cells along the cores and at the edge (RCPath G150)",
       "Usual-type epithelium: CK5/6 mosaic, ER heterogeneous",
       "B2 only when small and seen whole within the width of the core (RCPath G150)"
      ],
      "images": [
       {
        "src": "assets/reference/breast_biopsy/papilloma.jpg",
        "caption": "Intraductal papilloma in a large duct (H&E).",
        "credit": "Kulka et al., Virchows Arch 2022, Fig 2a (cropped)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8983543/"
       },
       {
        "src": "assets/reference/breast_biopsy/papilloma_p63.jpg",
        "caption": "p63 marks myoepithelial cells in the duct wall and along the fibrovascular cores of a papilloma.",
        "credit": "Kulka et al., Virchows Arch 2022, Fig 2d (cropped)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8983543/"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "Papilloma with ADH (B3) or DCIS (B5a)",
      "points": [
       "A monotonous atypical proliferation within the papilloma: CK5/6 lost, ER diffuse and strong",
       "ADH when the atypical area is 3 mm or less, DCIS when larger (RCPath G150)",
       "Intermediate or high nuclear grade: DCIS at any size (Kulka 2022)",
       "Myoepithelial cells are usually kept along the cores (RCPath G150)",
       "Atypia in a papilloma on a core: surgical excision is recommended (RCPath G150)"
      ],
      "images": [
       {
        "src": "assets/reference/breast_biopsy/papilloma_adh.jpg",
        "caption": "Atypical ductal proliferation under 3 mm within an intraductal papilloma: ADH (H&E).",
        "credit": "Kulka et al., Virchows Arch 2022, Fig 4a (cropped)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8983543/"
       },
       {
        "src": "assets/reference/breast_biopsy/papilloma_adh_ck5.jpg",
        "caption": "The atypical proliferation lacks CK5 staining.",
        "credit": "Kulka et al., Virchows Arch 2022, Fig 4b (cropped)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8983543/"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "Papillary DCIS (B5a)",
      "points": [
       "Delicate fibrovascular cores lined by monotonous atypical cells",
       "No myoepithelial cells along the cores, but a preserved layer around the duct (Rakha 2024; Kulka 2022)",
       "ER diffuse and strong, CK5/6 negative (Kulka 2022)"
      ],
      "images": [
       {
        "src": "assets/reference/breast_biopsy/papillary_dcis.jpg",
        "caption": "Papillary DCIS; the star marks a focus of microinvasion (H&E).",
        "credit": "Kulka et al., Virchows Arch 2022, Fig 5a (cropped)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8983543/"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "Encapsulated papillary carcinoma (B5a)",
      "points": [
       "Arborising papillae lined by low-grade cells in a cystic space with a fibrous capsule",
       "Myoepithelial cells are usually absent at the periphery, yet it is B5a (RCPath G150) and staged as DCIS (WHO 6th ed.)",
       "Most are ER positive and of low or intermediate grade; a high-grade or ER-negative one is rare, and a note of the unusual features is advised (WHO 6th ed.)"
      ],
      "images": [
       {
        "src": "assets/reference/breast_biopsy/epc.jpg",
        "caption": "Encapsulated papillary carcinoma: papillae lined by low-grade atypical epithelium within a cystic space and fibrous capsule (H&E).",
        "credit": "Kulka et al., Virchows Arch 2022, Fig 6b (cropped)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8983543/"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "Solid papillary carcinoma (B5a)",
      "points": [
       "Solid nodules of low-grade cells around fine fibrovascular cores",
       "Smooth, circumscribed nodules are in situ even without myoepithelial cells (WHO 6th ed.)",
       "Neuroendocrine differentiation and mucin production are very common (Kulka 2022)"
      ],
      "images": [
       {
        "src": "assets/reference/breast_biopsy/spc.jpg",
        "caption": "Solid papillary carcinoma: low-grade cells in a solid pattern filling dilated ducts (H&E).",
        "credit": "Kulka et al., Virchows Arch 2022, Fig 7a (cropped)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8983543/"
       },
       {
        "src": "assets/reference/breast_biopsy/spc_synaptophysin.jpg",
        "caption": "Synaptophysin expression in solid papillary carcinoma.",
        "credit": "Kulka et al., Virchows Arch 2022, Fig 7c (cropped)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8983543/"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "Invasive papillary carcinoma (B5b)",
      "points": [
       "Finger-like fibrovascular projections infiltrating desmoplastic or fibrotic stroma; exceptionally rare (Rakha 2026)",
       "No circumscription, capsule, neuroendocrine differentiation or mucin, unlike encapsulated and solid papillary carcinoma (Rakha 2026)",
       "Not for a non-papillary invasive carcinoma arising with papillary carcinoma in situ (Rakha 2026)"
      ],
      "images": [
       {
        "src": "assets/reference/breast_biopsy/invasive_papillary.jpg",
        "caption": "Invasive papillary carcinoma: cystically dilated spaces of varying size (H&E).",
        "credit": "Kulka et al., Virchows Arch 2022, Fig 8a (cropped)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8983543/"
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
